      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For clarification, basically you'd set your status based on each group of friends. Maybe set a \"lowest level\" for each group. So if I actually set my status to orange, I appear orange to everyone. But if Group 1's lowest allowed status is 'orange' and group 2's lowest is green, then group 3's is blue, I appear as orange for 1, green for 2 and blue for 1 if I set my actual status to blue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-02T17:21:17.427Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I love how you can set granular permissions to avatar settings based on a user's trust level. I wish I could do something similar with friends, where I have my main friend list that allows people to request an invite, as if I'm on orange status. But for my close friends who I have in a separate group, I'd like to appear as blue status, so they can join whenever they like.\nSetting granular permissions on join/invite requests would be really nice",
